From 41cf75d8f6de32f280c34530b3e22b777725226b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 03:00:35 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 061/230] Stop toasts sticking, and give Matchday honest empty
 states
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The stuck notification users hit on the Task card was not an ad bug: the toast
leave class `.toast-out` had no CSS rule at all, so the exit animation never
ran and its `animationend` — the only thing that removed a toast — never fired.
Every toast stayed on screen until a reload, three of them at a time. The leave
animation now exists, and the provider also reaps each toast on a timer so a
missing or undelivered event cannot strand one.

The Task card itself now has a failure policy: it collapses on the SDK's own
error events and on an error thrown out of the SDK script or a rejected promise
from it, and remembers for the session, so a route change cannot retry a block
Adsgram has already rejected. An unrelated page error leaves it alone and a
reload retries, so a fixed block id comes back on its own.

Matchday's own empty state was three empty sections on a fresh database. The
feed now renders one state at a time — a labelled skeleton list while the first
fetch is in flight, one error card if it failed with nothing cached, and one
centered empty state with a Sync now action when the sync has not filled the
feed yet. Previous results are always offered and name "No results yet" when
opened instead of vanishing. New copy ships in English and Persian.

POST /api/admin/sync already existed and was verified over HTTP (401 without a
token, 403 for a non-admin, { ok: true } when the sweep ran); the README now
shows how to call it.

